+---
+id: dl-001-rental-service-model-half-open-day-periods-sequential-booking-ids
+type: decision-log
+title: "Rental service model: half-open day periods, sequential booking ids"
+status: pending
+format: 1
+---
+
+## Context
+
+The school's rules require integer cents, UTC ISO-8601 times, whole-day bookings and no overlapping
+bookings of one item. The request leaves some details open.
+
+## Decision
+
+- A period is half-open `[start, end)`: `end` is the midnight after the last day, so back-to-back
+  bookings (one ends where the next starts) do not overlap. Total = number of days x `dailyPrice`.
+- Times are accepted only as UTC midnights written with a `Z` suffix (optional zero fraction); anything
+  else is rejected rather than silently converted. `quote`/`book` echo `start` and `end` as given.
+- Booking ids are sequential (`booking-1`, `booking-2`, ...) rather than random or clock-based, so the
+  service stays deterministic.
+- `addEquipment` rejects duplicate ids, unknown kinds, and a `dailyPrice` that is not a non-negative
+  integer.
+
+## Consequences
+
+A caller with local-time input must convert to UTC first. Ids are only unique within one service
+instance, which fits the in-memory scope. Cancellation will need to read a booking's start with the same
+parsing rules.
